    "preamble": "Ram Babu vs Govt. Of Nct Of Delhi And Ors. on 1 June, 2023",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "5. For the sake of completeness, the said terms and conditions attached to the Certificate of Vending, are reproduced herein below:- \"1. Vendor shall not have any other permanent or long-term vending certificate. 2. 8. Vendor/Squatter shall insure that no hindrance be caused to pedestrian and vehicular moment. Learned counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioner states, that he does not pray for the relief of running his business from any particular vending site, within the zone where he has been permitted to vend by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi, and further, the solitary relief that is prayed for, is to permit the petitioner to vend strictly, in accordance with the terms and conditions of the Certificate of Vending dated 08.11.2021, issued by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi. 7.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioner states, that he does not pray for the relief of running his business from any particular vending site, within the zone where he has been permitted to vend by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi, and further, the solitary relief that is prayed for, is to permit the petitioner to vend strictly, in accordance with the terms and conditions of the Certificate of Vending dated 08.11.2021, issued by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi. 7.",
